% Scenario: a 16x16 gray image whose data is a baseline JPEG stream
% read through currentfile /ASCIIHexDecode filter /DCTDecode filter.
% The samples are not decoded: the image reads the stream's bytes up
% to its end-of-image marker, the hexadecimal layer is read through
% its `>`, and the stream reaches the PDF verbatim under DCTDecode.
% The four 8x8 blocks are greys 128, 160, 224, and 160 in raster order.
% The stream is generated by `cargo xtask tiny-jpeg --corpus`;
% regenerate rather than edit.
100 100 translate
200 200 scale
%%BeginData: 8 ASCII Lines
<< /ImageType 1 /Width 16 /Height 16 /BitsPerComponent 8
   /ImageMatrix [16 0 0 -16 0 16]
   /DataSource currentfile /ASCIIHexDecode filter /DCTDecode filter >> image
FFD8FFDB00430001010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101
0101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101
01010101010101FFC0000B080010001001011100FFC400160001010100000000
00000000000000000000090AFFC4001410010000000000000000000000000000
0000FFDA0008010100003F002803400CFF00BFFFD9>
%%EndData
showpage
